    "title": "pandas.api.typing.SeriesGroupBy.tail — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1386.gcb2086a1a4 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.api.typing.SeriesGroupBy.tail#\n\n- \nSeriesGroupBy.tail(*n=5* )[source]#\n- Return last n rows of each group. Similar to `.apply(lambda x: x.tail(n))` , but it returns a subset of rows\nfrom the original DataFrame with original index and order preserved\n(`as_index` flag is ignored).\n  - Parameters:\n    - **n** int\n    - If positive: number of entries to include from end of each group. If negative: number of entries to exclude from start of each group.\n  - Returns:\n    - Series or DataFrame\n    - Subset of original Series or DataFrame as determined by n.\n See also \n  - `Series.tail`\n  - Apply function tail to a Series.\n  - `DataFrame.tail`\n  - Apply function tail to each row or column of a DataFrame.\n Examples >>> df = pd.DataFrame( ... [[\"a\", 1], [\"a\", 2], [\"b\", 1], [\"b\", 2]], columns=[\"A\", \"B\"] ... ) >>> df.groupby(\"A\").tail(1) A B 1 a 2 3 b 2 >>> df.groupby(\"A\").tail(-1) A B 1 a 2 3 b 2",
    "markdown_length": 906,
